{"archetypes":[{"name":"call-sites","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan changes exit behavior from nounset-abort to explicit exit 2; callers pattern-matching rc or stderr from these flags may break without an explicit call-site audit step in the plan.","prompt_body":"Check whether the plan includes a step to audit all existing invocations of `--partition-requested` and `--brainstorm-requested` in the repository. Locate every call site of `write-run-params.sh` and determine whether any downstream script or test inspects the exit code or error text when these flags receive bad input; a caller expecting rc=1 from nounset expansion would silently break after the change to rc=2. Verify the plan explicitly acknowledges or mitigates this behavioral contract change for each call site found. If the plan omits a caller-audit step or dismisses the breakage risk without evidence, that is a plan gap. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"test-helper-fidelity","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan asserts the four new tests validate rc==2, but does not verify that assert_rejected_with actually checks exit codes; if the helper only inspects stderr the rc guarantee is unfounded.","prompt_body":"Inspect the `assert_rejected_with` helper in `scripts/test-write-run-params.sh` and determine whether it verifies the process exit code (rc=2) in addition to the stderr substring match. If the helper only validates stderr output, the plan's testing-strategy claim that cases 'assert identical rc (2)' is inaccurate and the plan is missing an assertion or a helper-update step. Cross-check the plan's stated test guarantees against the helper's actual implementation contract. If the exit-code check is absent, flag this as a plan fidelity gap and note whether the plan should be amended or the helper extended. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
